Quick Setup Guide

1. Clone & Configure the Script
Download the script file into your current project folder containing your targeted application Dockerfile. Open the script file with a text editor (vim, nano) and configure the header setup variables according to your stack requirements:
Bash

IMAGE_NAME="your-custom-image"
CONTAINER_NAME="your-custom-container"
DOCKER_HUB_USER="your_dockerhub_account"
PORT=8080

2. Update System Permissions
To allow shell execution rights inside your Unix environment, assign the executable bits to the asset:

Bash

chmod +x docker-menu.sh

3. Execution
Launch the interactive orchestrator console using your preferred terminal interface:

Bash

./docker-menu.sh

 Enterprise Workflow Application Example
This operational tool serves as a secure bridge for Decoupled Architecture Releases. Developers can maintain private text structures on standard versioning spaces (e.g., private GitHub repositories), while utilizing this workflow automation client to push final, built immutable binaries over Docker Hub registries straight to runtime providers (e.g., Render, AWS, GCP).
This workflow pattern insulates master source repositories from infrastructure tokens, minimizing exploit surfaces in multi-tenant environments.

